   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2022 authorizing the Bellmore Fire\nDistrict to file an application for exemption from real property taxes, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6035-A and A. 6950-A, in relation to\nmaking technical corrections thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S2622",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2622-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.6035-A & A.6950-A)",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2622\n\nSPONSOR: RHOADS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2022 authorizing the Bellmore\nFire District to file an application for exemption from real property\ntaxes, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6035-A and A. 6950-A,\nin relation to making technical corrections thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nC.440.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by making technical\nchanges to the underlying chapter to ensure compliance with current law\nand to ensure proper local approval.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 13 of 2022, the Executive and Legislature\nreached this agreement to change the accepting entity from the town of\nHempstead to the Nassau County assessor, makes a technical change to the\nsection of law referenced, and provides that county legislature shall\nhave the power to approve the exemption at local option.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 440 of the Laws of 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date as a chapter of the laws of\n2022 authorizing the Bellmore Fire District to file an application for\nexemption from real property, as proposed in legislative bill number S.\n6035-A, takes effect.\n",
